    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\n`vim.hl.range()` computes a segment for every selected line, then discards all but the outer endpoints for characterwise and linewise highlights. This makes highlighting large yanks and puts unnecessarily expensive.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nUse `getregionpos()` with `bounds=true` for these highlights. Also use `bounds` in the keymap example that only needs the first and last selected lines.\r\n\r\n### Benchmarks\r\n\r\nLocal `vim.hl.range()` benchmark, averaged over 20 iterations. Each iteration creates the highlight, verifies its endpoints, and clears it.\r\n\r\n| Lines | Selection | Before | After |\r\n|---:|---|---:|---:|\r\n| 100 | Characterwise | 0.0949 ms | 0.0139 ms |\r\n| 100 | Linewise | 0.0806 ms | 0.0086 ms |\r\n| 100,000 | Characterwise | 68.7178 ms | 0.0156 ms |\r\n| 100,000 | Linewise | 66.1153 ms | 0.0163 ms |\r\n\r\nBefore and after produced identical highlight endpoints.",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-16T14:23:55Z",
